# etude-5dr.3 documentation impact

ANCESTOR: etude-5dr (P1) — issue #15 adds shipped workflow syntax, live-run
behavior, a failure mode, and manifest audit data that must be documented with
the caller-runner capability and guard.

BLAST RADIUS: documentation changes are limited to `docs/run.md`,
`docs/gates.md`, and the embedded `etude prime` reference in
`internal/cli/prime.go`. Generated command docs were checked but not rewritten.

TRUSTED INPUTS: the operator-selected workflow, installed Git executable, and
the caller directory's canonical repository identity, including configured Git
normalization/ignore/file-mode semantics. TRUST ROOT: committed Git HEAD/index
and repository-local controls captured before the runner. UNTRUSTED
INPUTS: runner output and ordinary runner filesystem effects until post-run
inspection succeeds. Arbitrary same-process code that replaces Git, forges Git
internals, or alters global tooling solely to deceive inspection is excluded;
caller mode is not a sandbox for hostile code already holding the operator's
permissions. Documentation limits the guarantee to synchronous completion under
exclusive working-tree access and does not claim serialization against unrelated
concurrent writers.

MEASUREMENT: the actual built CLI proof shows a clean caller commit succeeds with
manifest v4/post-run HEAD, while a zero-exit runner leaving a tracked mutation
exits nonzero and publishes no run ref. Automated regressions additionally prove
ambient worktree redirection and replacement refs cannot falsify inspection.

TOPOLOGY: one live producing runner may opt into caller workspace; all gate
checks/seats and replay paths remain hermetic. The docs keep those paths distinct.

DURABILITY CLASS: docs state the at-least-once crash/dirty residual, the
post-run committed SHA, and the pre-capture fail-closed boundary.

COMPLETENESS ENUMERATION: the relevant long-lived surfaces checked were live-run
behavior, gate manifest/version behavior, workflow/init schema reference, replay,
generated CLI references, README overview, embedded `prime` reference, and
planning-only product material.

IRREVERSIBLE SEQUENCE caller-runner: 1 steps
IRREVERSIBLE STEP caller-runner.1: invoke the authorized producing runner in the caller working tree

Crash residual: a runner may edit, delete, or commit before stage capture. A
crash leaves those observable effects and no run ref; resume is at-least-once,
so the operator must reconcile the tree and runners must be repeat-safe. Ignored
files are deliberately outside the tracked/non-ignored guard.

